Hi Gachie

On 03/11/15 08:22, gachie thomas wrote:
> My data is at child level (binary data), clustered at different clusters within counties and spans for period of 7 years. Some of the clusters within which child level data is collected are georeferenced while some are not.

You know from which of the counties each non georeferenced individual comes from?

> I need to fit a spatial-temporal model that can take into account the child level data, both the georeferenced data and the one that is not georeferenced, but make predictions at county level.

You can create a prediction scenario dataset (with NA in the outcome) and include in the fitting process. You have to include into it all the components in your model and the outcome column as well with NA's. When calling inla you them include it as data=rbind(mal.data.stunt, scenario.data).

Warning: You used Ntrials=dim(mal.data.stunt)[1] and it should be the number of trials for each observation. As you have individual dataset, does it has to be one? (one is the default value in inla).

